  "id": "opium",
  "term": "opium",
  "definition": "Opium is a substance with a major market in Asia that has long been viewed in some Asian cultures as a preventive or curative agent for illness; its old Persian name, Theriac, means antidote. In social-health discussions, it is noted both for widespread social harm and for ongoing, disputed beliefs that it can improve measures such as blood lipids, blood pressure, and blood glucose.",
